  "content": {
    "title": "When is Easter Sunday 2026? Here are the dates to know",
    "text": "Updated March 30, 2026, 3:29 p.m. CTApril is nearly here, and for many that means Easter is right around the corner.The Christian holiday can fall anywhere between March 22 and April 25, depending on the spring equinox and moon cycle. Here’s when Christians across Wisconsin will be celebrating Easter in 2026. When is Easter 2026? In 2026, Easter will be Sunday, April 5. Easter is when Christians celebrate the resurrection of Jesus Christ. Easter is considered the most important day in the Christian calendar. How is the Easter date determined? Easter Sunday is set on the first full moon following the spring equinox. The Catholic Church sets the spring equinox as March 21 every year. The schedule is based on the Jewish calendar of Passover and the subsequent moon cycle. In 2026, the Passover – sometimes called Paschal – moon appears April 1.The next Sunday after the April 1 Passover moon is April 5, the date for Easter. Orthodox Easter has a slightly later range of possible dates because the Eastern Orthodox Church uses the Julian calendar instead, USA TODAY reported. While it can fall between April 4 and May 8, Orthodox Easter will be on April 12 in 2026.When does Lent end in 2026? Lent began Feb. 18 and lasts until April 2. Lent begins on Ash Wednesday and starts a 40-day period of fasting and prayer ahead of Easter. When is Good Friday in 2026? Good Friday is on April 3, the Friday before Easter, in 2026. The Christian holiday is the marker of Jesus Christ’s death before his resurrection three days later on Easter Sunday. (This story was updated to add new information.)",
